## Positional Statement

For a user, today, Kivi is a tool to transcribe your voice and it is becoming a collaborator, 
then Partner that remembers what is about the user, likely to matter again, and safe to surface. 
Unlike memory systems that quietly learn from the user, Kivi learns from the user, who can change 
the preferences or facts remembered. It remembers stable facts, useful episodes, and repeated preferences, 
while never guessing, never overreaching, never rewriting the voice. Everything it remembers is visible, 
editable, honest, and when it does not know, it says so. Kivi is where memory and trust grow together, 
at the user's pace.
